"longitude":"0"},"name":"Sieve City/Closet","distance":"15","photoID":"0","difficulty":"IV+","approximate":false},{"type":"portage","description":null,"id":"100177","location":{"latitude":"0","longitude":"0"},"name":"Great Falls","distance":"16","photoID":"0","difficulty":"VI","approximate":false},{"type":"takeout","description":null,"id":"116952","location":{"latitude":"38.622","longitude":"-107.831"},"name":"Take Out","distance":"16","photoID":null,"difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false}],"alerts":[],"photos":[{"id":"881889","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"884544","description":"Bryan Ownen and Keith Kirchner enjoying a fall paddle in the Black Canyon of the Gunnison River. AW's work to quantify recreational flow needs throughout the Gunnison River Basin will help us protect boatable flows, even as water in the Southern Rockies becomes increasingly scarce. Photo: Chris Menges","caption":"Black Canyon","poi_name":null,"subject":null,"author":"Chris Menges","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/881889","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/881889"}},{"id":"5036","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"1022","description":"This is the 18 drop immediately before the big portage.  It's great fun. . .","caption":"18 footer at ~750 CFS","poi_name":"waterfall","subject":"Sam Lindblom","author":"Will Crim","poi_id":"100172","photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/5036","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/5036"}},{"id":"8032","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"7028","description":"One of the class V- rapids near the Narrows. Note that at this level, nothing was \"mandatory\". You can scout/portage pretty much all the hard stuff. However, this run is not recommended for class IV boaters nor for folks out of shape.","caption":"Black Canyon - Scott in the Narrows","poi_name":"Class V- rapid in the Narrows","subject":"Scott Willoughby","author":"Bryan Houle","poi_id":"100169","photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/8032","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/8032"}},{"id":"8027","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"7028","description":"Looking downstream at the main portage, as seen from the 18 footer.  The line is way up on the slope, tight to the cliff wall. It is an extremely strenuous portage and takes approximately 1.5 to 2 hours with a loaded boat. Take your time and try not to slip and get hurt. Your feet and legs are your biggest asset in this canyon!","caption":"Black Canyon - The Portage","poi_name":"Portage","subject":"none","author":"Bryan Houle","poi_id":"100177","photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/8027","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/8027"}},{"id":"8026","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"7028","description":"This rapid is around mile 2.5. Make sure to scout this one.  Identified by a sharp right turn in the river, followed by a left turn.  Go slow up until this point and eddy out early. Many sieves in this one. There's a large hole to the river left of the large rock in the center of the picture.","caption":"Black Canyon - Entrance to First V Rapid","poi_name":"Daywrecker (?)","subject":"none","author":"Bryan Houle","poi_id":"100168","photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/8026","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/8026"}},{"id":"8030","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"7028","description":"This is the rapid described in CRC as being a \"solid V above the 18 footer\". Not readily seen from the river right scout is a MAJOR sieve/cave on river right. Check this one out good and don't be too far right on the third drop or you might be surfed into the sieve.","caption":"Black Canyon - Solid V above 18 footer","poi_name":"Solid V above 18 footer","subject":"none","author":"Bryan Houle","poi_id":"100177","photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/8030","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/8030"}},{"id":"8217","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"7765","description":"This is the put in for the Black Canyon at East Portal.","caption":"Put In","poi_name":"n/a","subject":"","author":"Kit Davidson","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/8217","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/8217"}},{"id":"8229","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"7765","description":"Well put.","caption":"Warning","poi_name":"n/a","subject":"","author":"Kit Davidson","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/8229","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/8229"}},{"id":"888043","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"890875","description":"","caption":"Next Generation ","poi_name":null,"subject":null,"author":"Spencer Huff ","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/888043","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/888043"}},{"id":"891853","ext":"jpg","post_id":"895758","description":null,"caption":" on Gunnison @03. Crystal Dam to Chukar Trail ","poi_name":null,"subject":null,"author":null,"poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/891853","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/891853"}},{"id":"891854","ext":"jpg","post_id":"895759","description":null,"caption":" on Gunnison @03. Crystal Dam to Chukar Trail ","poi_name":null,"subject":null,"author":null,"poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/891854","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/891854"}},{"id":"891855","ext":"jpg","post_id":"895760","description":null,"caption":" on Gunnison @03. Crystal Dam to Chukar Trail ","poi_name":null,"subject":null,"author":null,"poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/891855","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/891855"}},{"id":"8025","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"7028","description":"","caption":"Black Canyon - 18 footer","poi_name":"18 foot waterfall","subject":"Bryan Houle","author":"Scott Willoughby","poi_id":"100172","photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/8025","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/8025"}},{"id":"8031","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"7028","description":"","caption":"Black Canyon - Paul 18 footer","poi_name":"18 footer","subject":"Paul Hemming","author":"Scott Willoughby","poi_id":"100172","photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/8031","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/8031"}},{"id":"8029","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"7029","description":"Although you might be sleeping on rock, you won't want to be any other place at this point.","caption":"Black Canyon - Rock Camp","poi_name":"Rock Camp","subject":"exhausted boaters/hikers","author":"Bryan Houle","poi_id":"100174","photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/8029","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/8029"}},{"id":"8028","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"7029","description":"Here's where you ferry across to river left to continue the portage. The river left portage takes about 30 minutes. There is an optional camp down here if you are ready to call it a day.","caption":"Black Canyon - Ferry Pool","poi_name":"Ferry Pool","subject":"none","author":"Bryan Houle","poi_id":"100161","photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/8028","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/8028"}},{"id":"41805","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"10083","description":"","caption":"Entrance to Daywrecker","poi_name":"Daywrecker","subject":"Kyle McCutchen","author":"Jake Zywicke","poi_id":"100170","photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/41805","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/41805"}},{"id":"41803","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"10083","description":"","caption":"Scouting Ballcrusher","poi_name":"Ballcrusher","subject":"","author":"Jake Zywicke","poi_id":"100174","photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/41803","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/41803"}},{"id":"41804","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"10083","description":"","caption":"Somewhere in the Narrows","poi_name":"Narrows","subject":"Kyle McCutchen","author":"Jake Zywicke","poi_id":"100156","photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/41804","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/41804"}},{"id":"427146","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"426854","description":"","caption":"Double Drop","poi_name":"Double Drop","subject":"Fremont Shields","author":"Matt Hopkins","poi_id":"100176","photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/427146","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/427146"}},{"id":"427211","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"426854","description":"","caption":"Pillow Move","poi_name":"Pillow Move","subject":"Fremont Shields","author":"Matt Hopkins","poi_id":"100162","photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medi